# Bedrock LLM — Admin Help chat and retail Ask (do not conflate)

## Two products, one model family

| Surface | Where it runs | Grounding | Call path |
|---------|---------------|-----------|-----------|
| **Retail / morning-brief Ask** | `adwiise-agent-ai-engine` `POST /v1/chat` | Saved brief JSON (metrics, cards, forecast) | Admin retail UI → Spring `/api/retail-brief/chat` → engine ALB → Bedrock |
| **Admin Help chat** | `adwiise-agent-admin` `POST /api/admin/help-chat` | Curated admin knowledge pack + pathname context | Floating Help on `/admin/**` → Next.js server → Bedrock **direct** |

- **Same account / model family:** `224674645062`, region **`us-east-1`** for Bedrock Runtime, default model `us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5`.
- **Different system prompts and context shapes.** Do **not** route Admin Help through the gas-station AI engine or `/v1/chat`.
- **Do not fine-tune** the model on admin pages. Prefer knowledge chunks + retrieval; update docs when UX changes.

## Admin Help architecture (canonical in agent-admin)

```
Admin UI (AdminHelpChat)
  → POST /api/admin/help-chat   (Clerk + ADMIN/SUPER_ADMIN)
  → retrieveAdminHelpKnowledge(question, pathname, isPlatformSuperAdmin)
  → Bedrock InvokeModel (or stub if BEDROCK_ENABLED=false / invoke fails)
```

Key paths (admin repo):

- Knowledge + retrieve: `src/lib/adminHelp/`
- API: `src/app/api/admin/help-chat/route.ts`
- UI: `src/components/admin/AdminHelpChat.tsx` (mounted from `AdminTenantContext`)
- Ops docs: `documentation/admin_help_chat/`
- Smoke: `npm run test:admin-help`

### Rules for Admin Help answers

- Use **only** retrieved knowledge + page context; never invent menu items or routes.
- Plain English how-to; read-only (no mutations).
- Omit `platformOnly` chunks for non–SUPER_ADMIN; refuse platform-only topics for ADMIN.
- Retail Ask on `/admin/retail` stays a **separate** UI/backend path.

## Env vars (local + Amplify)

```
BEDROCK_ENABLED=true
BEDROCK_REGION=us-east-1
BEDROCK_MODEL_ID=us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5
```

- Admin Help **defaults on** unless `BEDROCK_ENABLED=false` (or `ADMIN_HELP_BEDROCK_ENABLED=false`).
- Amplify Hosting apps are in **`us-east-2`**; Bedrock Runtime stays **`us-east-1`**.
- `amplify.yml` must grep `BEDROCK_` into `.env.production` at build time so SSR Lambdas see the vars.

